Frame-trace instrumentation: WebProcess composite marker (ATLANTIC_FRAME_TRACE).

Diagnostic-only (default OFF). When ATLANTIC_FRAME_TRACE=1, emit a
CLOCK_MONOTONIC-stamped "[ftrace] web composite" line at each
ThreadedCompositor::paintToCurrentGLContext. Paired with the qt5-plugin
"[ftrace] ui recv|paint|ack" markers (same clock), this brackets the
WebProcess->Qt handoff so the franceinfo "content freezes then jumps" stall can
be localized to production (composite stops), handoff/export (composite fires
but no ui recv), or present (ui recv fine but paint/ack lag). Live per-thread
sampling could not catch these random sub-second stalls; explicit frame timing
can. Zero cost when unset. Not shipped on.
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,8 @@
 #include <WebCore/TextureMapperLayer.h>
 #include <WebCore/TransformationMatrix.h>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <ctime>
 #include <cstring>
 
 #if USE(LIBEPOXY)
@@ -319,8 +321,28 @@
         layer->flushCompositingState(reasons);
 }
 
+// ATLANTIC_FRAME_TRACE=1: CLOCK_MONOTONIC-stamped marker at each WebProcess
+// composite, comparable to the qt5-plugin ui markers (same clock). Lets a
+// freeze-then-jump be localized: if 'web composite' keeps firing during a
+// screen freeze but 'ui recv' does not, the stall is in export/handoff; if
+// 'web composite' itself stops, the compositor is not producing (production
+// stall). Zero cost when unset.
+static bool atlFrameTrace()
+{
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const char* e = getenv("ATLANTIC_FRAME_TRACE");
+        return e && e[0] && e[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
